  "note": "Annual election of three members of the Holywood Urban Council, 16 May 1938; there was no contest (Belfast Telegraph, 7 May 1938, p. 13). The three outgoing members were Morrison, Seggie and Gillespie. Gillespie withdrew after nomination, and Morrison was returned unopposed with the two new members, A. E. Jefferson and J. M'Call, junior. The Northern Herald's report of the annual meeting welcomes the two new members, M'Call and Jefferson. Returned unopposed."
